public class Sleeper implements Runnable {

    @Override
    public void run() {
        try {
            Thread.sleep(3000);
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            System.out.println("error");
        }
    }
}

// Main
for (int i = 1; i <= 4; i++) {
    Thread t = new Thread(new Sleeper());
    t.start();
}

System.out.println("loop done");

How long after the program starts does loop done get printed?,"After about 3 seconds, once the threads have finished","Almost immediately - a few milliseconds. start() returns straight away and does not wait for the task, so main runs on while the threads sleep",After about 12 seconds,"It is never printed, because main is blocked by the threads",,2,"Measured at 3 ms. start() means 'begin this elsewhere and carry on', which is exactly why join() exists for the times you do need to wait.",2

