Four threads run Sleeper (3 s each) on a machine with just ONE core. How long until all four are done?,About 12 seconds - one core can only run one thread at a time,"Still about 3 seconds. Sleeping needs no core at all, so core count makes no difference to waiting",About 6 seconds,It depends on thread priorities,,2,"The dividing line again: waiting overlaps regardless of hardware. If Sleeper were computing fibonacci instead, one core really would force the work to take four times as long.",2

