Position (3) prints Thread.currentThread().getState(). What can that line ever print, and why?,"Any of the six states, depending on timing","RUNNABLE, always. You have to be running in order to execute the line that asks the question, so a thread can never catch itself in any other state","WAITING, because main has just come out of a join()","TERMINATED, because main is about to end",,2,"A genuinely useful thing to notice: getState() is only informative about OTHER threads. Asked about yourself, the answer is fixed.",2

